      "side": 1,
      "message": "i decided against enabling I2C_PORT_FLAG_DYNAMIC_SPEED on ppc1\nbecause i don\u0027t intend to enable speed change capability\non ppp1 in general. we really only need to \"patch\" the speeds\non board ID 1 and if/when we drop support for board ID 1,\nwe can remove set_board_legacy_i2c_speeds ugliness.\n\nyes, we are changing speed at runtime here, but this is a very\nrestricted form. it happens right after the I2C controllers\nare initialized but before most I2C devices are used.\ni think CBI is the only exception. i actually\ndoubt i2c_lock() is even needed here, but i couldn\u0027t prove\nit to myself.\n\ni originally started mimicking the CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_RUNTIME_CONFIG\ndesign pattern for i2c_ports[],\nbut that presented its own complexities because\nthis array is accessed very early - before we know the board ID\nas that comes from CBI (I2C PROM).\n\nthoughts?",
